CAPCAF: Context-Aware Privacy Compliance and Adaptation Framework
Overview
CAPCAF is a hybrid design-time and runtime framework for adaptive privacy-utility optimization in Internet of Things (IoT) environments. This is the initial public release accompanying the manuscript "A Hybrid Design-Time and Runtime Framework for Adaptive Privacy-Utility Optimization in IoT."

What's Included
Core Framework Modules
Domain Configuration Interface (DCI): Template-based configuration for Healthcare, Smart Home, and Industrial IoT domains.
Design-Time Phase:
Threat Modeling and Taxonomy (model inversion, data poisoning, side-channel, inference, re-identification)
Context and User Modeling (PUTC behavioral trade-off)
Threat Injection and Simulation Environment
Performance and Regulatory Constraint Modeling (HIPAA, GDPR, PIPL)
Multi-Objective Policy Optimization (NSGA-II + Q-learning)
Policy Validation and Stress-Testing
Runtime Phase:
Real-Time Context Acquisition (RTCA)
Real-Time Signal Processor and Feature Extractor
Adaptive Risk Quantification (PUTC Calculator)
Runtime Adaptation Manager (RAM)
Runtime Policy Execution Engine (RPEE)
Monitoring and Continuous Adaptation:
Monitoring and Logging
Online Learning from Feedback
Policy Adaptation
Design-Time Refinement
Cross-Domain Scalability Mechanisms
Output Interfaces and Consumers
Experimental Artifacts
NSGA-II configuration: 500 generations, population size 100, 100 independent runs
Run-level statistics (mean privacy risk, mean utility, mean threat risk, best utility)
Baseline implementations: Static_DP (LATENT), Context_Agnostic (IoTWatch), Domain_Specific
Ablation study configurations
Datasets Supported
Smart Home: CASAS dataset (50 sensors/actuators, 12 contextual variables)
Healthcare: Synthea™ synthetic cohort (200 patient profiles, 25 contextual variables)
Industrial IoT: MIMII dataset (machine sound telemetry, vibration data, anomaly patterns)
Requirements
Python 3.13.0
NumPy 2.4.3
Pandas 3.0.1
SciPy 1.17.1
TensorFlow 2.21,0
Pymoo 0.6.2
PyTorch 2.10.0
